    <string name="manual">Manual</string>
    <string name="manual_sub">How everything in Sign works</string>
    <string name="manual_intro">Tap a chapter to open it, or search.</string>
    <string name="manual_search">Search the manual</string>
    <string name="manual_version">Manual for Sign v%1$s</string>
    <string name="manual_start_t">Getting started</string>
    <string name="manual_start_b">1. Open Settings (the gear at the top right) and draw your signature by tapping the white field under Signature 1. Fill in your name and press Save.\n2. On the home screen, choose Photograph document or Open document.\n3. Tap Signature, then tap where it should go on the page, and sign.\n4. Press Save, choose a format and share the file.</string>
    <string name="manual_scan_t">Photograph a document</string>
    <string name="manual_scan_b">Photograph document opens a scanner that finds the edges of the paper by itself. You can take several pages, adjust the corners and retake a page. The result becomes a PDF that you can sign right away.</string>
    <string name="manual_open_t">Open a document and formats</string>
    <string name="manual_open_b">Open document shows your Download folder. Sign reads PDF, Word (.docx and old .doc) and OpenDocument (.odt), and recognises the format by itself. You can also open a file from another app with Open with or Share to Sign, for example an email attachment. A password-protected PDF asks for the password.</string>
    <string name="manual_place_t">Place signature, photo and stamp</string>
    <string name="manual_place_b">Tap Signature, Photo or Stamp at the bottom and then where it should go on the page. Drag to move it, drag the corner to change the size and tap the cross to remove it. A stamp can be rotated with the gold handle or the slider (−45° to 45°, ±5°). The chosen stamp is placed in the top left corner of the first page automatically. Signing is done in landscape so there is room to write.</string>
    <string name="manual_sigs_t">Signature 1, 2 and 3</string>
    <string name="manual_sigs_b">In Settings each signature has a preview. Tap the white field to write or change the signature – it opens with what you drew before, so you can redo just part of it, for example the surname. Use ↶ Undo and Redo ↷ to step back and forward, and Clear to start over.\nSignature 2 is optional and also can be photographed on paper or taken from a file (PNG, JPG, BMP or WEBP); the paper becomes transparent.\nYou choose whether the name, the date (always today\'s) and the photo are shown next to the signature. Before a saved signature is used, Sign asks whether to use it, change it, take a new photo or skip the photo.</string>
    <string name="manual_who_t">Who signs</string>
    <string name="manual_who_b">Under each signature you fill in who signs: name, email and phone. Press Save – the button shows Saved. Save as contact adds the person to Contacts, and Choose from Contacts fills in the fields. When you place a signature in a document you choose who signs: one of your signatures or a contact who signs directly on this phone.</string>
    <string name="manual_save_t">Save as</string>
    <string name="manual_save_b">Press Save in the document. Give the document a name and choose Save as a new copy if the original should be kept. Tap one or more formats – PDF, Word, ODT, or one image per page (PNG or JPG) – and press the big gold button. A PDF keeps its text; PDF to Word or ODT puts the pages in as images. An old .doc can become a real Word file with editable text.</string>
    <string name="manual_saved_t">Saved documents</string>
    <string name="manual_saved_b">All documents are saved, even unfinished ones, with a picture of the first page. In the corner: green Sign 1 2 means that signature fields 1 and 2 are signed; red Unsigned means no field is signed yet. Tap ⓘ for an explanation. Tap a document for a large preview where you swipe between pages and see who is missing. From there you can continue signing, rename, share or delete.</string>
    <string name="manual_share_t">Share</string>
    <string name="manual_share_b">Share sends the file to WhatsApp, Gmail, Drive and other apps, to a contact, or saves it in Download. If you saved several formats, Sign first asks which one to share, or all of them.</string>
    <string name="manual_stamps_t">Stamps and logos</string>
    <string name="manual_stamps_b">Under Settings → Stamps you choose the stamp for the top left corner. Import logo or Photograph logo opens the image tool:\n• Crop: drag the corners.\n• Remove background: removes the background connected to the edges; the slider removes less or more.\n• Erase and Restore: draw with your finger; choose the size.\n• Colour: tap a colour to remove it, only the connected area or everywhere.\n• ↶ Undo and Redo ↷, pinch to zoom, two fingers to move.\nWhat remains keeps its colours and the rest becomes transparent. Preview on checkered, white paper or dark. Your own logos can be edited again with ✎. Tip: for an icon on a computer, a screenshot gives the sharpest result.</string>
    <string name="manual_camera_t">The camera</string>
    <string name="manual_camera_b">The camera takes pictures in the highest quality and focuses by itself. Tap the screen to focus on a spot, pinch with two fingers to zoom and double-tap to go back to 1×. The picture is taken when it is sharp. The front camera is the default for photo and signature; many front cameras cannot focus close up, so use the back camera for paper and logos.</string>
    <string name="manual_contacts_t">Contacts</string>
    <string name="manual_contacts_b">Contacts are listed A–Z with search, and quick buttons for email and calls. Swipe to delete (with Undo) or press and hold to select several. With sync turned on, the phone\'s contacts with email or phone are shown, and changes are saved both ways. When deleting you choose Only from Sign or Also from the phone.</string>
    <string name="manual_updates_t">Updates</string>
    <string name="manual_updates_b">When a new version exists, New updates appears at the bottom of the home screen and a gold dot on the gear. Update in Settings → Updates. What\'s new shows every version; tap a version to read what it contains.</string>
    <string name="manual_language_t">Language</string>
    <string name="manual_language_b">English is the default. Choose Swedish under Settings → Language. The document scanner and the Android file picker follow the phone\'s language.</string>
</resources>
